1 NAME Gustav /Plaut/
2 GIVN Gustav
2 _MARNM Plaut
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 FEB 1824
2 ADDR
3 CITY Nordhausen
3 STAE Thuringia
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 JUL 1908
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hamburg
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Bankier
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gustav's father Herz Cusel PLAUT (1784, January 29, 1837) was from Reichensachsen. The bank "HC Plaut" was founded in Nordhausen  in 1815 after his marriage to Caroline Blach (1800-1874) from Abberode. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustav PLAUT, (1824-1908) moved to Leipzig in 1852 and became a director of the bank. As a banker, he advised the Prince of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen and the Duke of Saxe-Meiningen . Gustav was also in 1865 made an honorary citize
2 CONC n of Nordhausen. In the War of 1866, he disguised himself as a peasant and saved the King of Saxony's treasure against looting by the Prussians. He hid the gold bullion under a layer of potatoes in a cart which he drove through th
2 CONC e Prussian lines. For this he was awarded the Royal Order of Fourth Class. He retired in 1875 and moved to Hamburg shortly before 1890.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustav Plaut was born on 26 February 1824, the fifth child and third son of Herz C Plaut, and Caroline (née Blach), from Reichensachsen (near Eschwege) on the border between Thuringia and Hesse. He became a banker who funded trade
2 CONC  with Russia and Poland as well as a number of railways. He also rescued the King of Saxony’s gold and jewels from the advancing Austrian army
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustav_Plaut
