1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Date/place of birth in record of birth in Hessisches Staatsarchiv Marburg. http://tinyurl.com/4kye4pf9. The German National Archives has been informed of the error in the entry re: birth date/place for Frieda Löb
2 CONC enstein. (December 2023)
2 CONT * Identified as daughter of Abraham and Jette (née Selig) Hirsch in birth record cited above
2 CONT * Identified as wife of Leopold Löbenstein in record of their marriage on 03 April 1912 in Bischhofsheim; see http://tinyurl.com/bdhzrksd
2 CONT * Please Note: The entry in the database compiled by Dr. Siegfried Wolf, ''Juden in Thüringen 1933-1945: Biographische Daten''. (2000), vol 1, p. 354, is incorrect. Frieda Hirsch was not the wife of Bernhard Löbenstein, but was th
2 CONC e wife of Leopold Löbenstein.
2 CONT * Identified as mother of  Horst and Elfriede Löbenstein in Yad Vashem Pages of Testimony
2 CONT * On 10 May 1942, Frieda Löbenstein was deported from Weimar to Belzyce Ghetto with her daughter, Elfriede.
2 CONT * Stolpersteine were laid for Leopold and Frieda (née Hirsch) Löbenstein in Mühlhausen/Thüringen in 2013. Stolpersteine for their children- Irmgard, Horst, Arno, Elfriede, und Liselotte Löbenstein-were laid in March 2015 in Mühlha
2 CONC usen/Thüringen; https://www.muehlhausen.de/rathaus-erkunden/erinnerungsorte/stolpersteine-in-muehlhausen/herrenstrasse-5/#c24785. See as well: http://muehlhausen.thueringer-allgemeine.de/web/lokal/politik/detail/-/specific/Elfried
2 CONC e-Loebensteins-Laecheln-kam-ueberraschend-zurueck-2065871057
2 CONT
2 CONT Entry in [https://www.bundesarchiv.de/gedenkbuch/en843552 German National Archives, ''Memorial Book'']':<br/>
2 CONT '''Loebenstein, Frieda'''<br/>
2 CONT née Hirsch born on 1885 in Wanfried / Eschwege / Hessen-Nassau<br/>
2 CONT resident of Mühlhausen i. Thüringen<br/>
2 CONT Deportation:<br/>
2 CONT from Weimar-Leipzig<br/>
2 CONT 10th May 1942, Belzyce, ghetto<br/>
2 CONT Date of death: 1942<br/>
2 CONT Place of death: Distrikt Lublin
