1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Date of birth identified on Stolperstein laid for Irmgard Löbenstein in Mühlhausen/Thüringen. This is 5 years earlier than the date in the attached document.
2 CONT * Identified as daughter of Leopold and Frieda Löbenstein in Stolpersteine documents; see below.
2 CONT * In December 1939, Lieselotte Löbenstein sailed on the same boat, the Hilda, to Palestine with her sister, Irmgard. Irmgard died in an accident on board ship; Lieselotte immigrated into Palestine.
2 CONT * She was interned in the Atlit detainee camp. The Wikipedia entry tells us: "The Atlit detainee camp was a concentration camp established by the authorities of Mandatory Palestine in the late 1930s on what is now the Israeli coas
2 CONC tal plain, 20 kilometres (12 mi) south of Haifa. Under British rule, it was primarily used to hold Jews and Arabs who were in administrative detention; it largely held Jewish immigrants who did not possess official entry permits.[
2 CONC 1][2] Tens of thousands of Jewish refugees were interned at the camp, which was surrounded by barbed wire and watchtowers."
2 CONT * Stolpersteine were laid for Leopold and Frieda Löbenstein in Mühlhausen in 2013. Stolpersteine were laid for Irmgard, Horst, Arno, Elfriede, und Liselotte Löbenstein in March 2015 in Mühlhausen/Thüringen;  https://www.muehlhause
2 CONC n.de/rathaus-erkunden/erinnerungsorte/stolpersteine-in-muehlhausen/herrenstrasse-5/#c24785. See as well: http://muehlhausen.thueringer-allgemeine.de/web/lokal/politik/detail/-/specific/Elfriede-Loebensteins-Laecheln-kam-ueberrasch
2 CONC end-zurueck-2065871057
