1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Prof. Dr. Hugo Carl PLAUT (1858-1928) 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1882 he received a degree in veterinary medicine from the University of Leipzig and subsequently studied medicine in Leipzig and Kiel. He remained in Leipzig working as a practicing doctor and biological researcher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1894 he discovered the cause of Plaut-Vincent angina. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to the University of Hamburg in 1897 where he served as professor working in the grounds of the Eppendorf hospital affiliated Plautsche Research Institute for Bacteriology. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Adele Brach (b.1864 d.1954) in 1888
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugo Plaut
