1 NAME Louis /Eliel/
2 GIVN Louis
2 _MARNM Eliel
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 FEB 1826
2 PLAC Iba, Hesse
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 MAY 1884
2 PLAC LaSalle Illinois
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louis Eliel was born in 1826 in Iba, Hesse, the 5th of 6 children. He came to America as a young adult and [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:9392-919M-K?i=256&cc=1614804&personaUrl=%2Fark%3A%2F61903%2F1%
2 CONC 3A1%3AZZGY-41ZM on October 26, 1856, married his first cousin, Minka Danziger, in Cincinnati, OH.] Their mothers were  sisters, daughters of Lamm Eliel and Hanna Plaut. Minka came to Baltimore in 1834 when she was 3 years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "The Way It Was: The Jewish World of Rural Hesse" (published 2000), both arranged marriages and marriages between cousins were quite common among the Jews of rural Hesse. So cousins Louis Eliel and Minka Danziger may 
2 CONC have had an arranged marriage. (At least 2 of Louis Eliel's siblings also married their first cousins.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis and Minka moved to Chicago, Illinois in 1856 immediately after their marriage. There they raised 9 children. Louis went into business with his younger brother, Jeremiah, who had started a brewery in LaSalle, Illinois in 1854
2 CONC . The LaSalle business directory of 1877 lists "L. Eliel and Company, Brewers of Lager Beer. Chicago Office :247 Lake Street." It states that the brewery was producing over 100 barrels a day and employed 30 hands. Apparently the E
2 CONC liel brewery had their own railroad cars to carry barrels from LaSalle to Chicago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis died May 8, 1884 in LaSalle, probably while visiting his brother Jeremiah. Minka died March 31,1899 in Chicago. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/170808111/louis-eliel They are buried in Rosehill Cemetery, Chicago.]   
