1 NAME Jeremias /Eliel/
2 GIVN Jeremias
2 _MARNM Eliel
1 NAME Jeremias /Eliel/
2 GIVN Jeremias
2 SURN Eliel
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 FEB 1828
2 ADDR
3 CITY Iba, now Bebra
3 STAE Hessen
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 AUG 1897
2 PLAC LaSalle Illinois
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jeremiah Eliel, the youngest of six children, was born in Iba Hesse in 1828. As a young man he went to America, and when he was 26 started his own brewery in LaSalle, Illinois. The LaSalle town directory of 1877 li
2 CONC sts him as a brewmaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Jeremiah was 32 he married a 17-year-old Lutheran, Alwine Struever, who had come to America from the Kingdom of Hanover (Germany) with her parents when she was 10 years old. Their marriage took place October 19, 1860 in LaSal
2 CONC le, where her parents lived. About three years after Jeremiah's marriage, Alwine's mother became a widow. She spent most of the rest of her life living with Jeremiah and Alwine and helping them raise their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah and Alwine raised 7 children in LaSalle. Their children were Protestant Christians. Their 4th child, Elfriede, married her first cousin, Edwin Eliel whose father, Louis,  was Jeremiah's brother and partner in the brewery.
2 CONC  This is why we are descended from both Louis Eliel and Jeremiah Eliel but we are Christian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah Eliel died in LaSalle on August 26, 1897. Alwine Struever Eliel died April 29, 1915. They are buried in LaSalle. 
