1 OCCU kaiserlich ottomanischer Generalkonsul, Honorary Consul General for the Turkish Empire in Debrecen and later Vienna.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.barrow-lousada.org/PDFdocs/DeDirsztayTreeP2.pdf Honorary consul General for the Turkish Empire in Debrecen and later Vienna.    '''19/4/1899 Dropped surname Fisch/Fischl, retaining Dirsztay alone.'''    
2 CONC '''30/11/1905  made Baron de Dirsztay by Emperor Franz Joseph.'''    Commissioned and lived at Dirsztay Palace in Vienna & Budapest. '''m1 Etelka Steinfeld''' b Debrecen 4 Apr 1861 d Budapest 28 Mar 1943. They were divorced. Etelk
2 CONC a married secondly Count Ernö Zichy de Vasonkeö '''m2 Georgina Plaut'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.barrow-lousada.org/ '''LASZLO 1860-1922 as the grandson of LAZAR 1772-1841''' We have suggested they were not father (IGNASZ 1825-1907) and son (IGNASZ 1845-19170 but that the older Ignasz was the son of LAZAR Fischl an
2 CONC d the younger Ignasz was the son of LAJOS/LAZAR Fischl. Lajos is a Hungarian equivalent of Lazar. In this way we show Lajos 1870-1932 as the grandson of Lajos Fischl 1798-1856, and '''LASZLO 1860-1922 as the grandson of LAZAR 1772
2 CONC -1841'''.    Online sources suggest to him that Bela's father Gutmann had a father named Moses not Lajos, that the father of Moses was Lazar Eleazar Fischl b~1772 in Timisoara, and an Ignasz was a brother of Moses Fischl. On the o
2 CONC ther hand, we point to the probability that Laszlo 1860-1922 was the grandson of Lazar, and hence that Gutmann was the son of Lazar not Moses. We retain the Moses suggested by Scott McDougall as a grandson of Moses bar Baruch aka 
2 CONC Moritz Baruh. Moritz is an equivalent of Moses. Perhaps Bela is an echo of Baruch, the father of Moritz Baruh, and the (suggested) unknown brother of Lazar 1772-1841 would have been named Baruch if he was the oldest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
