1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rahel Liebeschütz-Plaut
2 CONT * Famous People Throughout History
2 CONT * Birth:	June 21 1894 - Leipzig, Germany
2 CONT * Death:	Dec 22 1993
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rahel_Plaut
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr Rahel Plaut (1894-1993) was a medical doctor and researcher in physiology who became the first female academic to be appointed at Hamburg University School of Medicine. Between 1919 and 1924 she co-authored 25 scientific papers
2 CONC  on subjects including metabolism, muscle physiology and infectious disease. She married the historian Hans Liebeschuetz (German: Liebeschütz) in Hamburg in 1924. They emigrated to England in 1938 to escape Nazi persecution
2 CONT
