1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Neither religious nor church-going, Frieda had long-standing (Dellevie) Jewish ancestry.  Based on her regional reputation as a classical pianist, she chose to stay in Kassel even after her husband Hermann Weiler w
2 CONC as murdered by the Nazis in December, 1939. But the Nazis made things ever tougher and Frieda escaped in 1942 with her brother Theodor Dellevie and his wife Olga.  Incredibly at age 61, they made their way mostly on foot across oc
2 CONC cupied France, then free-France, then by horse-drawn cart over the Pyrenees then Spain and into neutral Portugal. After several delays they booked passage to Cuba, but Theodor -- exhausted -- died on shipboard. Frieda and Olga con
2 CONC tinued to Colombia, worked there for many months, then Frieda was permitted entry to the USA. She joined my family in Dallas in 1943.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Steven M. Fulda (grandson)
