1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joel S Weissman, 1953, Cambridge, MA, Wendy,  10/13/1953, Gideon 1986, Aaron .
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Abner Landman, 1962, wife and children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jessica Catherine and Martin Mullaney with Conor and Michael.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Otto Landmann's history of the Landmanns, 1984 (text is relative to 1984).
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Ernest * 1925. Married to Ruth Hallo * 1926 in 1948. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto is Professor of Biology (Genetics) at Georgetown  University. Ruth is Professor of Anthropology at  American University, Washington, D.C. They have  three children.  Wendy Anne * 1953. Married to Joel Weissman * 1953 in 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1981. Wendy is in Urban Planning. Joel is in Health  Planning -currently attends Brandeis University working  towards a Ph.D. They live in Cambridge, MA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jessica Catherine * 1954. Jessica is in her third year  at Georgetown University Law School. She also has  a job in a Law Firm and is editor of a Law Journal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Abner * 1962. Jonathan is currently in his senior  year at Brandeis University. He spent his junior  year in China. First improving his Chinese and,  more recently, teaching English at Nanjing University.  (see Genealogic
2 CONC al Tables for overview). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In June 1982 Jonathan joined a group of students from  Duke University for study in China. He spent one semester  in Beijing and the second part of the year in Nanjing, where  he found a job for himself to teach English to Univers
2 CONC ity  students and to Graduates who want to go to the U.S. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth and Otto travelled to China in June 1983 to share  Jonathans last month in China with him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ‐---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Obit for Martin Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Loving Memory of Martin J. Mullaney 
2 CONT
2 CONT August 4, 1934- December 16, 2019 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin J. "Marty" Mullaney Sr., 85, of Cambridge, Md. passed away peacefully at his home and went home to Heaven on Monday December 16, 2019. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marty was born on August 4, 1934 to Thomas and Catherine Mullaney in Cumberland, Md. He enjoyed a wonderful childhood in Cumberland and after graduating from LaSalle High School in Cumberland, Md. he attended Duquesne University o
2 CONC n a basketball scholarship. He was drafted into the Army in 1954 and served in Korea for two years. He then attended Mount Saint Mary's College and studied History. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In October 1959 he married the love of his life, Kathleen Marie "Kathy" Carney of Cumberland, Md. They had three children together-Cammy, Marty and Ricky. He was a loving husband, a devoted father and granddad. Early in his career
2 CONC  he worked for Met Life and in March 1963 he and his family moved to Cambridge, Md. where he worked in Life, Health, Property and Casualty Insurance. He started his own insurance agency, Mullaney Insurance Inc. in 1979. Marty and 
2 CONC Kathy worked together every day until her death in January 1993. Their daughter, Cammy, joined them in 1991 and their son Marty joined them in 1997. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was very involved in his Church St. Mary's Refuge of Sinners. He served on the Parish Council, the Finance Council and he was a Eucharistic Minister. He was on the Union Trust Advisory Board and he was a member of several clubs
2 CONC : VFW, American Legion, Elks, Cambridge Country Club, Cambridge Yacht Club, and the Dorchester Chamber of Commerce, he was a Board member of the George B Todd Foundation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a longtime member of the Cambridge Rotary Club where he served on the Board for many years which culminated in being President of the Club 1984-1985. He was the President of the Rotary Scholarship fund for many years. He wa
2 CONC s a Paul Harris Fellow and was awarded the Rotary Lifetime Achievement Award in December 2012. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a long time Board member and Finance Committee member and very involved with Delmarva Community Services. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marty was always willing to give of his time and talent. He took up golf later in life and really enjoyed the sport and the friendships he made along the way. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marty is survived by his daughter, Cammy and her husband Tom, his son Marty and his wife Jessica and their two sons Conor and Michael, and his son Rick and his wife Marie and their four children Sam, Zach, Katie and Josh. He is al
2 CONC so survived by his brother Tom and his wife Shirley, his sister Rosemary and her husband Gene and his sister Kathy and her husband Joe, several nieces and nephews, many cousins and many friends. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents and his loving wife, Kathy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pall Bearers will be his five grandsons- Conor, Michael, Sam, Zach and Josh Mullaney and his son-in-law Tom Tyson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A Celebration of Life will be held on Monday December 23, 2019 at St. Mary's Refuge of Sinners at 11AM. Friends will be received at the church an hour and a half before mass. A second service will be held on Friday, December 27, 2
2 CONC 019 at 11 am at Saints Peter and Paul Catholic Church, 125 Fayette Street, Cumberland, MD 21502 with family receiving friends from 10 to 11. Interment will follow at St. Peter and Paul Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers contributions can be made to St. Mary's Refuge of Sinners, 2000 Hambrooks Blvd., Cambridge, MD 21613, Delmarva Community Services, 2450 Cambridge Beltway, Cambridge, MD 21613, Cambridge Rotary Club, P.O. Box 703
2 CONC , Cambridge, MD 21613 or Coastal Hospice Foundation, P.O. Box 1733, Salisbury, MD 21802.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements are in the care of the Thomas Funeral Home, P.A. in Cambridge, MD.
