1 NAME Werner /Frank/
2 GIVN Werner
2 _MARNM Frank
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 JAN 1902
2 ADDR
3 CITY Marburg an der Lahn
3 CTRY Alemanha
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 NOV 1948
2 ADDR
3 STAE Montevideo
3 CTRY Uruguay
1 BURI
2 DATE ABT 21 NOV 1948
2 PLAC Cemitério São João Batista
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rio de Janeiro
3 STAE RJ
3 CTRY Brasil
1 OCCU Import Export Handler
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Werner worked for his father at the Leather Company 'SALAMANDER' in Frankfurt since very young until he was in his middle 20's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated from Frankfurt a.Main, Germany to Rio de Janeiro, Brazil in the middle 20's, first alone (although already being married since the age of 23 to Margarete Frank (born Levi), but 2-3 years later returned to Germany to pick
2 CONC  her up and bring her to Rio de Janeiro, where they lived first in Ipanema (Av. Epitacio Pessoa, 433), then as of 1935 in Leblon (Rua Timóteo da Costa, 32).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Werner was an Import/Export Man and founded 'Importadora Werner Frank' at Rua Julia Lopes de Almeida, 18 in downtown Rio de Janeiro.  The company used to import all different goods but later concentrated on shoe machines from Denm
2 CONC ark, watches from Switzerland (Oris Brand) and Needles for Tissue making Machines.
2 CONT
2 CONT Werner was on a vacation trip to Montevideo, Uruguay with his wife Margarida (Margarete) in November 1948 (at the age of 46) when suffered a heart attack in Montevideo and was brough to a local hospital for 2-3 days, where died. H
2 CONC is body was embalmed and brought to Rio de Janeiro mid-end November 1948, where was burried at the São João Batista Cemetery in Botafogo, Rio de Janeiro
