1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hans Liebeschuetz
2 CONT * Jewish Holocaust Memorials and Jewish Residents of Germany 1939-1945
2 CONT * Birth:	Dec 3 1893 - Hamburg / - / Hansestadt Hamburg
2 CONT * Death:	Oct 2 1978 - Merseyside
2 CONT * Residence:	Hamburg, Hansestadt Hamburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Liebeschütz
2 CONT * Famous People Throughout History
2 CONT * Description:	German Historian
2 CONT * Birth:	Dec 3 1893 - Hamburg, Germany
2 CONT * Death:	Oct 2 1978 - Crosby, United Kingdom
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Liebfschuetz
2 CONT * England & Wales, Death Index, 1837-2005
2 CONT * Death date:	Oct-Nov-Dec 1978
2 CONT * Death place:	Crosby, Merseyside, England
2 CONT * Birth date:	Mar 1893
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Liebeschutz
2 CONT * United Kingdom, Jewish Death and Burial Records
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1894
2 CONT * Death:	Oct 28 1978 - London, England [INCORRECT]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Jewish Chronicle - Nov 10 1978
2 CONT
2 CONT Prof Hans Liebeschuetz
2 CONT
2 CONT Professor Hans Liebeschuetz, the historian and medievalist, has died in Liverpool.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Liebeschuetz, writes Dr Arnold Paucker, director of the Leo Baeck Institute, was born in Hamburg in 1893 and after receiving his doctorate from Heidelberg University was for many years a teacher of classical languages in his 
2 CONC native city and at the same time a lecturer in medieval Latin at Hamburg University.
2 CONT
2 CONT Driven from school and university posts by the .Nazis, and after some years as lecturer at the Hochschule fuer die Wissenschaft des Judentums in Berlin under Rabbi Dr Leo Baeck, he emigrated in 1939 with his family to England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He again became a schoolmaster before moving to Liverpool on being appointed lecturer, later reader, in medieval history at Liverpool University.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the honours bestowed on him in the 1960s in Germany was that of a professorship at Hamburg University.
2 CONT
2 CONT He wrote extensively both on the intellectual history of the Middle Ages and on Judaism. He was a founder of the Leo Baeck Institute and made., many important contributions to its work on German-Jewish history.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/c/F41159
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.nli.org.il/en/a-topic/987007299512105171
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hUR7YWUb0k0
