1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hermann Weiler was my grandfather; I knew him well during the 1930s in Kassel, Germany. Although not religious (only two records of his attendance at the local synagogue between 1930 and 1938) the Gestapo took him 
2 CONC on Kristallnacht. He was murdered 12½ moths later, leaving his very successful coffee distributorship to us children and grandchildren.  Sadly, the Nazis eventually got most of the company "Carl Weiler Kaffee". Carl Weiler was Her
2 CONC mann's father.
