1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/16279173/heinrich-spitzer FindAGrave]
2 CONT
2 CONT The German says:
2 CONT
2 CONT Engineer of the [Austro-Hungarian] Imperial and Royal Northern Railway [Nordbahn]
2 CONT born January 29, 1845
2 CONT died June 9, 1896
2 CONT
2 CONT Peace be with his ashes
2 CONT
2 CONT Into the place of our bliss
2 CONT Deep sorrow has come
2 CONT Our sun has gone out
2 CONT Robbed from us what we venerated
2 CONT Dearest one with the noble heart
2 CONT You were our sun
2 CONT Remain unforgettable in joy and in pain
2 CONT May eternal rest slumber gently.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hebrew says:
2 CONT צבי שפיטצער בר נתן.
2 CONT ''Tz’vi Spitzer, son of Nathan''
2 CONT ‎נולד כו &lbrack;כ״ו, 26&rbrack; שבט תרה &lbrack;תר״ה, 5605&rbrack; ונפטר כח &lbrack;כ״ח, 28&rbrack; סיון תרנו &lbrack;תרנ״ו, 5656&rbrack; לפה.
2 CONT ''Born on the 26th of Shevat, 5605 and died here &lbrack;Linz, Austria&rbrack; on the 28th of Sivan, 5656.&ast;''
2 CONT
2 CONT &ast; Note: the Hebrew birth date is actually [https://www.hebcal.com/converter?gd=3&gm=2&gy=1845&g2h=1 3 February, 1845], not 29 January.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Followed by a Biblical acrostic poem that (almost) spells out Heinrich’s Hebrew name:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT תנצבה &lbrack;תנצב״ר&rbrack;
2 CONT ''May his soul be bound to the bundle of life ([https://mechon-mamre.org/p/pt/pt08a25.htm 1 Samuel 25:29]), roughly a much more poetic R.I.P.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation railroad engineer per marriage records of daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Cornelia-Taussig/6000000176113395840 Cornelia]. These records also list his parents’ names as Nathan Spitzer and Anna (no maiden name liste
2 CONC d).
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth records of his daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Rosa-Martinez/6000000217905182900 Rosa] also say Heinrich was registered in Skotschau/Skoczów, meaning he was likely born there. 
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/16279173/heinrich-spitzer Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 11 2025, 0:08:21 UTC''
