1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Anschel Elkan Wasserman (son of Elkan Regensburger (Wassermann) and Rechl) was born 1774 in Harburg, Germany, and died September 25, 1833. He married Perl Steinhardter.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Notes for Anschel Elkan Wassermann: Anschel owned a leading bank in Germany centered in Harburg, under the name A.E. Wassermann. He was the starter of a banking family and the Feuchtwanger family is still known today as a famous 
2 CONC banking family. The Harburg bank's doors was open at the beginning of every week until Anschel felt he had enough money to live for that particular week. When his goal for each week was reached, he would close up the bank and go h
2 CONC ome and learn Torah for the rest of the week. There were times that he closed it on Thursday and there were times that he closed it on Tuesday. 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Anschel Elkan Wassermann: Occupation: Wealthy Merchant Banker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anschel Elkan Wassermann and Perl Steinhardter are:  +Fanny Wassermann, b. February 26, 1799, Wallerstein, Germany, d. July 5, 1875, Fürth, Germany. David Wassermann. Samuel Wassermann. Heimann Wassermann. Elkan Wasser
2 CONC mann. Sofie (Sprintele) Wassermann. Regine (Rechele) Wassermann. Dolze Wassermann.
2 CONT  http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/s/t/r/Jonathan-Strauss-New-Jersey/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0087.html
