1 OCCU Professor of Botany
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.tidhar.tourolib.org/tidhar/view/5/2293 אנציקלופדית תדהר]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%9C_%D7%90%D7%95%D7%A4%D7%A0%D7%94%D7%99%D7%99%D7%9E%D7%A8 ויקיפדיה עברית]
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillel_Oppenheimer '''Hillel Oppenheimer'''] (Hebrew: הלל אופנהיימר‎, born 'Heinz Reinhard Oppenheimer' 4 April 1899, died 1971), was an Israeli professor of botany.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oppenheimer was born in Berlin, Germany in 1899. His father was Franz Oppenheimer, a German-Jewish sociologist and political economist. Between 1917 and 1922, Oppenheimer studied botany at universities in Berlin, Frankfurt and Fre
2 CONC iberg in Germany and at the University of Vienna in Austria, where he received his doctorate.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the invitation of Selig Suskin, Oppenheimer emigrated to Mandate Palestine in 1925, and for some years was actively involved in attempts to establish new settlements and drain the swamps around Zichron Yaacov.
2 CONT
2 CONT In about 1931, he commenced working as a physilogist in the Department of Botany at the Hebrew University of Jerusalem. He helped found the Faculties of Natural Science and Agriculture at the university, and was their first lectur
2 CONC er on the subjects of anatomy and physiology of the plant. From 1933 to 1941, Oppenheimer headed the Department of Physiology and Genetics of the Agricultural Research Station in Rehovot. From 1941 to 1953, he was head of the depa
2 CONC rtment for the growth of citrus tree and agricultural botany, being appointed as a professor in 1949. Oppenheimer was dean of Faculty of Agriculture at the Hebrew University from 1953 to 1954.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1959, Oppenheimer was awarded the Israel Prize, in agriculture.
