1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Selly unusually for a Jew, rose to the rank of officer in the German army during 1st World War. He Left germany sometime before the 2nd World war for Amsterdam Holland accompanied by his step-mother, Regine.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Flat 4 Johannes Verhul? Murillo, Amsterdam but his last address was given as Corelli Strasse, Amsterdam. It was probably from here that he was arrested. He was sent to a detention camp at Westerbork on 10th Setember 19
2 CONC 42 and then transferred to Auschwitz on 14th September 1942. It is assumed that he died on or near that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
