1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Albert was born in Wallensen, Kreis Hameln and moved to Hanover in 1888 where he attended the Realgymnasium I Hannover then to Reifezeugnis fur den Einjahrigan Freiwilligen Dienst. In about 1901 he went to Vereinig
2 CONC ten Wollworen Fabriken in Marienthal, Hameln (3 years technical school), followed by Webschukle, Achen? 1905-6 and 4 years study in USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert founded a carpet factory in Hameln Germany in August 1910 with his partner Ernst Josephs (later to emigrate to Sao Paulo Brazil with his family). The factory was called Otto Kuhlman & Co, Teppichwerk GmbH (presumeably named
2 CONC  after the previous owner).  He lived at 21 Kaiserstrasse, Hameln, (the house still exists, according to Barbara Andrusz who has recently visited there). There is still a factory on the same site.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert was conscripted into the German Army in 1916 during the 1st World War (Infantrie Regiment 74), Hannover. He was sent to the Russian front and was wounded by bullet in the upper arm. The bullet travelled close to his heart a
2 CONC nd was considered inoperable, he nevertheless survived with it until the end of his life. He was released by the army at the end of the war in 1918. The factory had been idle during bthe war, but it slowly restarted after Alberts 
2 CONC return. Its operation was satisfactory until 1934 and was sold under Nazi pressure and in October 1935, he moved with his wife and daughters Hilde and Ursula to Berlin. He had already sent his daughter Eva out of Germany to finish
2 CONC ing school in Lausanne, Switzerland in about 1935. He asked and received permission to take his family with him on a business trip out of Germany, and left for Holland on 1st April 1936 and in the same month to England.
2 CONT
2 CONT In England he lived with his family at 39 Armitage Road, Golders Green (acquired in 1938). The house was hit by an incendiary bom during the 2nd World War sustaining minimal damage to the roof. Albert had kidney failure and was ta
2 CONC ken to hospital to have it removed. Soon after being taken away in in ambulance the police came to arrest him in order to confine him in a detention camp for foreign nationals. He avoided this fate by being in hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
