1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Hannchen Schonholz, the wife of  Falk Rosenstein was born in Lutgeneder.  That town is VERY close to  Borgentreich. All the Shonholz family came from Lutgeneder and  they died there.   That doesn't mean that they 
2 CONC were  BURIED there.  Apparently the Jews of Lutgeneder were  buried somewhere outside the city limits. "
2 CONT
2 CONT We were out of town, driving through the countryside on little roads.  It was grassy everywhere.  From time to time, as we were driving, we would see some trees, a short distance off  the road.  Each time, we pulled off to the sid
2 CONC e of the road and walked  over to where the trees were.  
2 CONT
2 CONT There, beneath the trees were gravestones with Hebrew lettering!   It was so quiet and serene.... out in the countryside, nothing around but grass and some dirt roads, and  in the midst of it a few trees with jewish gravestones be
2 CONC neath them".  
