1 OCCU Manufacturer, goldsmith, soap-boiler, and later owner of margarine factory E. Feuchtwanger in Haidhausen near Munich, Germany, MANUFACTURER; GOLDSMITH, SOAP-BOILER, -MARGARINE (E. FEUCHTWANGER FACTORY)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elkan's great granddaughter (Elsbeth Elias) married his great nephew (Eli Hackenbroch).
2 CONT
2 CONT He had various professions. Manufacturer, goldsmith, soap boiler, margarine manufacturer. His margarine company situated in Haidhaussen near Munich, had branches in Rumania, Holland and Egypt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elkan Feuchtwanger (1823 - 1902)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Furth, Germany on 30 Dec 1823 to Seligmann Feuchtwanger and Fanny Vogele Wasserman. Elkan married Sarah Further and had 7 children. He passed away on 4 Jun 1902 in Munich, Germany.
2 CONT
