1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Allene T. Plaut Is Dead at 83; Ex-Associate Editor of Vogue Published: March 15, 1986 SIGN IN TO E-MAIL PRINT
2 CONT
2 CONT Allene Talmey Plaut, a former associate editor and columnist at Vogue magazine, died Tuesday at her home in Manhattan. She was 83 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before joining Vogue in 1936, Miss Talmey, who used her maiden name professionally, had been the managing editor of Conde Naste's original Vanity Fair magazine. Earlier, she had been a reporter with The New York Morning World and 
2 CONC The New York Evening World, the associate editor of Stage magazine and a film reviewer for Time magazine.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a columnist for Vogue for more than three decades and was associate editor from 1963 to 1971. She also headed the magazine's feature department. After retiring in 1971, she became a contributing editor to Vogue, reviewing 
2 CONC books and writing profiles of medical and political figures She was a native of Brookline, Mass., and a graduate of Wellesley College.
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Talmey's husband, Richard L. Plaut, died in 1974. She is survived by a son, Richard L. Jr., of Manhattan; a sister, Georgia Talmey Colin of Manhattan, and two grandchildren.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/person-3196007_176795891_176795891/allene-plaut-born-talmey MyHeritage Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 27 2018, 4:11:49 UTC''
