1 OCCU Businessman - Harts Mountain Pet Food Company. Founder Stern College, Entrepreneur, Businessperson
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Max_Stern_(businessman)
2 CONT
2 CONT Max Stern (1898–1982) was an entrepreneur who established and built the Hartz Mountain Corporation, which eventually became one of America's most-successful privately held companies.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Fulda, Hesse, Germany, to parents Emanuel and Caroline Stern. He emigrated to the United States in 1926.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a leading Jewish philanthropist, he helped many charitable organizations both in the U.S. and Israel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stern founded the Stern College for Women — the undergraduate women's college of arts and sciences of Yeshiva University, located in New York City, New York, which is associated with Modern Orthodox Judaism — with a major grant, i
2 CONC n honor of his late parents Emanuel and Caroline Stern.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Max Stern Academic College of Emek Yezreel, located in Jezreel Valley, Israel, is named after him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stern was a communal lay leader.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1982, age 83, leaving his son, Leonard N. Stern, to carry on the family business.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Max_Stern_%281%29
2 CONT
