2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	May 20, 1982
2 CONT
2 CONT New York New York County New York, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Max Stern (1898–1982) was an entrepreneur who established and built the Hartz Mountain Corporation, which eventually became one of America's most-successful privately held companies. He was born in Fulda, Hesse, Germany, to parent
2 CONC s Emanuel and Caroline Stern. He emigrated to the United States in 1926. As a leading Jewish philanthropist, he helped many charitable organizations both in the U.S. and Israel. Stern founded the Stern College for Women — the unde
2 CONC rgraduate women's college of arts and sciences of Yeshiva University, located in New York City, New York, which is associated with Modern Orthodox Judaism — with a major grant, in honor of his late parents Emanuel and Caroline Ste
2 CONC rn. The Max Stern Academic College of Emek Yezreel, located in Jezreel Valley, Israel, is named after him. He died in 1982, age 83, leaving his son, Leonard N. Stern, to carry on the family business. He is interred in the Sharon G
2 CONC ardens Division of Kensico Cemetery.
2 CONT
