2 CONC C''
2 CONT
2 CONT ANNE LIBERMAN FORMERLY OF GARY, INAnne Liberman, one of Gary, Indiana's early residents, passed away Wednesday, March 12, 2008 in Orlando, FL. She was preceded in death by her husband of 29 years, Irwin Liberman. 
2 CONT Mrs. Liberman was an active resident and member of the Kinneret Senior Community in Orlando, FL since the year 2000 and until her passing. Prior to her move to Orlando, she was a resident of Laguna Woods, CA for 16 years where she
2 CONC  lived in retirement as an active and vibrant participant in the Leisure World Community. Prior to that she lived in Miami, FL for a period of 10 years where she worked for Sax Bal Harbour Department Store. 
2 CONT Mrs. Liberman, the oldest of six children, was born to Aaron and Ida Bornstein on April 17, 1917. She was the proud mother of three sons. She leaves behind six grandchildren and 10 great-grandchildren. 
2 CONT Mrs. Liberman is being returned to Gary, IN to be laid to rest next to her husband, who died as a result of gunshot wounds suffered during an unsolved robbery attempt on his store, March 7, 1966. Mr. Liberman subsequently lingered
2 CONC  in a coma for five days before he expired. 
2 CONT Beth Shalom Memorial Chapel of Orlando, FL has been entrusted with the preparations for Mrs. Liberman's return to her hometown for burial. Graveside services will be held Friday, March 14, 2008 at 1:00 p.m. at Temple Beth El Cemet
2 CONC ery in Portage, IN. Rev. Raphael Ostrovsky officiating. Burns Funeral Home, 10101 Broadway, Crown Point, IN in charge of arrangements.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/269375057/anne-liberman Find A Grave Memorial]
