3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Arthur Eliel was born at his maternal grandparents' home in LaSalle, IL, but grew up in Chicago. His parents Edwin and Elfriede were first cousins, both born Eliels. Their fathers were brothers, Louis and Jeremiah 
2 CONC Eliel,  who had come from Iba, Hesse, in the 1850's and started a brewery in LaSalle with distribution in Chicago. His paternal grandmother, Minka Danziger Eliel (widow of Louis Eliel and also his first cousin), lived with Art Eli
2 CONC el's parents in Chicago. She died in 1899 when Art was 6 and his brother Bob was 10. She spoke only German, and so they learned German at home before they learned English, although their parents had been born in the United States 
2 CONC and educated in English.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Eliel received a Bachelor of Science degree in architecture from The Armour Institute of Technology (now Illinois Institute of Technology, Chicago) on May 28, 1914. He worked as an architectural draftsman in Chicago for a f
2 CONC ew years.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was drafted into the U.S. Army effective April 29, 1918. (The U.S. had entered the World War against Germany in April, 1917.) Art served most of his time in the 30th Artillery, Coast Artillery, at Fort Munroe, Virginia. He beca
2 CONC me a 2nd lieutenant on September 25, 1918, about 6 weeks before the war ended on November 11, 1918.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1920 - 1932 he and his brother Robert Eliel, also an architect, had their own successful business designing private homes in Rockford, Illinois. This ended during the Great Depression.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1935 he found work as an architect with the federal government in Washington, D.C. In 1940 he was married to Margaret Doyle, a woman from Massachusetts who had also come to Washington to work for the federal government during t
2 CONC he Great Depression. They were married for 22 years (until his death in 1962), lived in Virginia and Massachusetts, and had one daughter. Arthur Eliel and his wife are buried in Arlington National Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT
