1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Karl Carl "Charles" SCHIFFERES: b. 22 Oct 1894, Wien - d. circa August 1942, Auschwitz, HOLOCAUST
2 CONT
2 CONT Already clearly accomplished as a cellist at the tender age of eleven - as shown by this mention of a recital featured in a newspaper of the era, viewable courtesy of:
2 CONT
2 CONT ANNO, Neue Freie Presse, 1905-11-09, Seite 12 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://anno.onb.ac.at/cgi-content/anno?aid=nfp&datum=19051109&query=%22karl+schifferes%22&ref=anno-search&seite=12
2 CONT
2 CONT Did he later (also) play the guitar?
2 CONT
2 CONT Details of deportation and subsequent death courtesy of:
2 CONT
2 CONT www.doew.at
2 CONT
2 CONT Vorname: Karl Nachname. Schifferes Geburtstag: 22.10.1894 Geburtsort: Wien Wohnort: Wien 18, Khevenhüllerstrasse 20
2 CONT
2 CONT Deportation. Drancy/Auschwitz Deportationsdatum: 26.08.1942
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicht überlebt
2 CONT
2 CONT Quelle: Shoah-Opfer
2 CONT
2 CONT And also ...
2 CONT
2 CONT http://db.yadvashem.org/names/nameDetails.html?itemId=4002076&language=en
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dokumentationsarchiv des österreichischen Widerstandes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * First Name Karl
2 CONT * Last Name Schifferes
2 CONT * Date of Birth 22.10.1894 (incorrect)
2 CONT * Place of Birth Wien
2 CONT * Residence Wien 18, Khevenhüllerstrasse 20
2 CONT * Deportation Drancy/Auschwitz
2 CONT * Date of Deportation 26.08.1942
2 CONT
2 CONT Plus ...
2 CONT
2 CONT https://yvng.yadvashem.org/nameDetails.html?language=en&itemId=4002076&ind=0
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Schifferes was born in Wien, Austria in 1894 to Leopold and Hermine. He was a musician and married to Gisela nee Pieringer. Prior to WWII he lived in Wien, Austria. During the war he was in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Carl was murdered in the Shoah.
2 CONT
2 CONT This information is based on a Page of Testimony (displayed here) submitted by his nephew, Stephan Shiffers Schifferes
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Name Schifferes  First Name Carl  Gender Male  Age 45  Date of Birth 1894  Place of Birth Wien,Vienna,Austria  Father's First Name Leopold  Mother's First Name Hermine  Marital Status Married  Spouse's First Name Gisela  Spou
2 CONC se's Maiden Name Pieringer  Permanent Place of Residence Wien,Vienna,Austria  Profession Musician  Place during the War France  Place of Death Auschwitz,Camp,Poland  Status according to Source murdered  Submitter's Last Name Shiff
2 CONC ers  Submitter's Last Name Schifferes  Submitter's First Name Stephan  Relationship to Victim Nephew  Source Yad Vashem - Pages of Testimony Names Memorial Collection  Type of material Page of Testimony  Item ID 4002076 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mémorial de la Shoah
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ressources.memorialdelashoah.org/notice.php?q=noms_tous%3A%28laufer%29%20AND%20id_pers%3A%28%2A%29&spec_expand=1&rows=20&start=27
2 CONT
2 CONT Features actual list of deportation (shown here under "Media"
2 CONT
2 CONT In David Jakob MATZNER's memoir (with David MARGOLIS) of his years as prisoner he writes of a spontaneous recital by a trio of musicians who had just arrived "from Vienna" (in fact, they had been deported from Drancy in France but
2 CONC  were all, indeed, of Viennese origin).
2 CONT
2 CONT Surely there were other Viennese musicians who were deported from Drancy to Auschwitz; however, the three musicians about whom Matzner wrote were not Laufer, Steissel and Schifferes. Laufer, true to his name, was able to run away 
2 CONC during a transfer.. Steissel was sent to KZ Gross Rosen and Schifferes was murdered shortly after his arrival in KZ Auschwitz..So the information provided below pertains to some other Viennese musicians, of which there were surely
2 CONC  many who were attempting to escape the Nazis  by fleeing to France. But not the three from the G.T.E. as claimed below.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi David Jakob Matzner (1904 - 1986) - Genealogy
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi David Jakob Matzner
2 CONT
2 CONT May his words speak further ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Viewable courtesy of the Center for Jewish History - digital collections - at the Leo BAECK Institute, New York: RLAUFER: DigiTool - Results - Full
2 CONT
2 CONT http://digipres.cjh.org:1801/delivery/DeliveryManagerServlet?dps_pid=IE8558344
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 29 (39 of pdf)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Three professional musicians from Vienna had also arrived. Their instruments - a violin, an accordian and a guitar - were kept in the guard house, for often they were called to entertain the guards. Whenever music came from there
2 CONC , I thought that Schubert, Strauss and Mozart would turn in their graves had they known what murderous creatures their compositions now pleased.
2 CONT
2 CONT One evening, the three musicians were permitted to play for us prisoners. An empty barrack had been prepared with long benches, with seats reserved for Davidowitch, Cohen, the capos, the kitchen personnel, and women from the offic
2 CONC e. There was singing, some dancing, a couple of instrumental and vocal solos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cohen had asked, the violinist, to play the Andante Cantalistene of Tschaikovsky's Violin Concerto. Laufer's violin sang in deep, sonorous tones, and silence fell over us. Men and women bent their heads, some with tears in their e
2 CONC yes. Deeper than ever before, I felt the loss of my life, the waste of hopes and ideals, of goals I dreamed of achieving. I thought of my parents, my brothers, my sisters, of the brutal destruction of God-given beauty and talents.
2 CONT
2 CONT The violinist finished. Before applause could begin, his voice and features full of bitterness, he said, "I should have broken that piece of wood before they got me." Markiel, the shoemaker, peppy as always, replied, "What do you 
2 CONC mean? We expect you to lead us out of here with this music. You are our Pied Piper."
2 CONT
2 CONT i.e. Associated with the following GENI profiles:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rudolf "Rudi" Laufer (1904 - 1992) Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Rudolf-Rudi-Laufer/6000000088025482967
2 CONT
2 CONT &
2 CONT
2 CONT Fritz Steissel (1919 - 1996) - Genealogy
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Fritz-Steissel/6000000003182200021
2 CONT
2 CONT (pip - Feb 2019)
2 CONT
2 CONT A few further welcome details thanks to the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Documents - Caisse 4
2 CONT
2 CONT http://judaisme.sdv.fr/histoire/shh/dordogne/caiss4/caiss4.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT "L'affiche placée à l’arrière plan sous la photo du chef de l'Etat français annonce un gala présenté par l’équipe artistique des Travailleurs Etrangers au profit de l'Oeuvre du colis au prisonnier, au Casino de Paris, à Périgueux,
2 CONC  les 22 et 23 avril 1942. Ils se produisent aussi à Bergerac. Cette équipe artistique a été formée par des Travailleurs Etrangers du 653e GTE d'Egletons et du 665e GTE Juif de Soudeilles (Corrèze). Elle organise, durant l'hiver 19
2 CONC 41-1942, des tournées en Corrèze, Dordogne et Haute-Vienne et elle associe danseurs et chanteurs autrichiens et espagnols. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Quatre solistes juifs tiennent la vedette sur l'affiche : un violoniste autrichien, Rudi Laufer, qui dirigeait l'ensemble, un violoncelliste de l'opéra de Vienne, Carl Schifferes, deux pianistes de la radio de Vienne, Frédéric Ste
2 CONC issel et Kurt Weininger. La proximité, sur le même mur, de Pétain et de ces artistes juifs ne doit pas faire illusion. Les succès de cette équipe ne plaisent pas à tout le monde. Les rafles d'août 1942 disloquent l'équipe, Frédéri
2 CONC c Steissel et Carl Schifferes sont déportés à Auchwitz par le convoi n° 24 du 26 août 1942, Kurt Weininger est déporté à Maïdanek par le convoi n° 51 du 6 mars 1943, Rudolf Laufer sauve sa vie en parvenant à fuir. Le Commissariat 
2 CONC général aux questions juives étudie le projet de reconstitution du groupe à partir d'effectifs non-Juifs et conclut ainsi son rapport : "[Le groupe artistique] reflètera alors la valeur des Travailleurs Etrangers aryens, qui ont u
2 CONC ne autre allure et une autre ardeur au travail que les Juifs, qui ne cherchent qu'à éviter maladroitement tout travail manuel." (Rapport n° 676 du 28 août 1942. Arch. dép. Haute-Vienne, 985 W 454)."
2 CONT
2 CONT Rough summary: Four Jewish musicians gave solo performances at gala events organised by the "Foreign Workers Committee" in April 1942. Austrian violinist Rudi Laufer was also head of the group. Carl Schifferes was a cellist at the
2 CONC  Vienna Opera. The two pianists who played for Vienna radio were Frédéric Steissel and Kurt Weininger.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was erroneously it is stated that Rudolf Laufer "escaped" (unless this refers to a later escape from concentration camp ...?).
2 CONT
2 CONT  This is  NOT an erroneous statement. Steissel and Laufer were transferred to  other concentration or work camps since they were much younger than Schifferes, who was sent to KZ Auschwitz. During  one of these transfers, Laufer wa
2 CONC s p, in fact, able to escape.
2 CONT
2 CONT A photo shows a poster of one of these gala events, featuring the names of these musicians.
