1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dawid Spitzer built the leather factory Spitzer (later Skotan) in 1859 when he was 26.<br/>
2 CONT http://www.skotan.com.pl/index.php?strona=10&jezyk=2<br/>
2 CONT ....1859 marked the arrival of Dawid Spitzer in Skoczów. This 26-year-old man from Cierlicko near Cieszyn most probably made use of the Industrial Regulations and started his own tannery shop in Skoczów. Over the years the shop gr
2 CONC ew into a big tannery processing different kinds of raw material into footwear, clothing and furniture leather, using vegetable tanning agents only. The formation of "Spitzer-Sinajberger" partnership around 1928 led to a further, 
2 CONC conspicuous development of tanneries in Skoczów. ....
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in this passage translated from Polish from [http://cmentarze-zydowskie.pl/wilamowice.htm the Jewish cemeteries of Poland] website:
2 CONT
2 CONT > On December 21, 1892, the Land Government in Opava notified the Bielsko County Office of the establishment of a new Jewish community in Skoczów. Its board included ''Dawid Spitzer'', Heinrich Tramer, [https://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Leopold-Lindner/6000000028116194156 Leopold Lindner], Wilhelm Spitzer, and Dr. Otto Hoffenreich. On July 19, 1893, [https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Dr-Lieber-Dobsch%C3%BCtz/6000000002342350417 Dr. Lieber Dobschütz], a graduate 
2 CONC of the Jewish Theological Seminary in Wrocław, was elected the first rabbi of Skoczów.
2 CONT
