2 DATE 1 FEB 1945
2 PLAC Todesmarsch von Auschwitz nach Buchenwald
2 ADDR
3 CITY Blechhammer
3 STAE Sachsen
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Kaufmann; Direktor der Schuhfabrik Lingel in Erfurt
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eintrag im »Gedenkbuch« des Bundesarchivs:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Spier, Karl Carl Ludwig geboren am 15. Dezember 1900 in Köln / - / Rheinprovinz wohnhaft in Erfurt
2 CONT
2 CONT * Inhaftierungsort: 11. Mai 1940, Brüssel, Gefängnis St. Gilles Saint Cyprien, Internierungslager
2 CONT
2 CONT * Emigration: 19. November 1935, Belgien
2 CONT
2 CONT * Deportationsziel: ab Drancy 02. September 1942, Auschwitz, Vernichtungslager
2 CONT
2 CONT * Todesdatum/-ort:  01. Februar 1945, Todesmarsch
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Carl Ludwig SPIER: b. 15 Dec 1900, Köln/Cologne - d. 1 Feb 1945, "Todesmarsch von Auschwitz2, HOLOCAUST
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Details of deportation and subsequent death courtesy of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl & Hilde SPIER were in the region of Nice, Côte d'Azur, where they were rounded up in the notorious "Rafles d'août" in August 1942. The arrested Jewish citizens were incarcerated in the Caserne Auvare for a while before being 
2 CONC put on a goods train, in locked-up wagons, and transferred to Drancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT cf. Archives Départémentales des Alpes Maritimes:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.basesdocumentaires-cg06.fr/os-html/adam/home.html
2 CONT
2 CONT SPIER "Charles": Infirmerie Hommes, Voiture 8
2 CONT
2 CONT SPIER Hilde: Infirmerie Femmes, Voiture 9
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT i.e. it appears both were unwell - whether possibly self-inflicted state because of fear of arrest is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also cf. listing thanks to:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://niceoccupation.free.fr/rafle-daout-1942.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Details of further deportation and subsequent death courtesy of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mémorial de la Shoah
2 CONT http://ressources.memorialdelashoah.org/notice.php?q=noms_tous%3A%28laufer%29%20AND%20id_pers%3A%28%2A%29&spec_expand=1&rows=20&start=27
2 CONT
2 CONT On Hilde's page many further details are given.
2 CONT
2 CONT - the family had first fled to Belgium.
2 CONT
2 CONT - she was a "journalist"
2 CONT
2 CONT - together with their two children the couple lived at Cap d'Ail before capture and deportation.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Features family group photo plus actual list of deportation (shown here under "Media")
2 CONT
2 CONT Convoi # 27
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT cf.: http://hoerstolpersteine.net/dr-hilde-spier-und-carl-ludwig-spier-erfurt/
2 CONT
2 CONT &: http://juedisches-leben.erfurt.de/jl/de/heute/erfurter_gedenken/orte/index.html
2 CONT ----
2 CONT NOTE
2 CONT Bundesarchiv Gedenkbuch contains these two entries:
2 CONT - Spier	Karl Carl Ludwig	15.12.1900	Köln	
2 CONT - Spier	Carl	15.12.1900	Köln	
2 CONT Both are shown as deported to Auschwitz 02.09.1942.
2 CONT We make the assumption that the entries are duplicated.
