1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kind:	 Louis de Vries Moeder:	 Betje van Strien Vader:	 Aaron de Vries Geboortedatum:	 31-03-1874 Geboorteplaats:	 Rotterdam
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruidegom:Louis de VriesGeboorteplaats:RotterdamBeroep:KoopmanVader bruidegom:Aaron de VriesBeroep:KoopmanMoeder bruidegom:Betje van StrienBruid:Clara DalbergGeboorteplaats:Niedermarsberg (Duitsland)Vader bruid:Alex DalbergMoeder 
2 CONC bruid:Emilie HeinemannGebeurtenis:HuwelijkDatum:vrijdag 18 augustus 1899Gebeurtenisplaats:Niedermarsberg (Duitsland)
2 CONT
2 CONT Overledene Louis de Vries diversen zoon van Vader Aaron de Vries Moeder Betje van Strien Relatie Clara Dalberg Gebeurtenis Overlijden Datum 26-07-1958 Gebeurtenisplaats Veghel
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.pondes.nl/detail/inddetail%20ENG.php?inum=753790420
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.pondes.nl/detail/sfinfo.php?sour=1440594990&naam=
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.famillebutlerdelarochelle.com/devries.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis de Vries was born in Rotterdam. He became a well-to-do businessman, owning a chain of hosiery stores (shirts, gloves, etc). Having moved to Amsterdam, he built a fine house around 1910, bordering the small lake of the Vondel
2 CONC  Park. Louis was a kindly man, apparently too much so in fact, so that he seems to have been taken advantage of and couldn't cope with the thirties' economic crisis. After which his business declined.
2 CONT
2 CONT On August 22, 1899 Louis de Vries married Clara Dalberg at the Elberfeld Synagogue in Germany. They had 3 children: Alexandre (Lex) and twins Bob and Betsy (known as "Zus"- meaning "sister") 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Holland was invaded on 10 May 1940, Lex fell on the third day of hostilities. Clara passed away a few days earlier . After that, being Jewish , Louis kept a low profile, and finally was taken into the safe harbour of a cathol
2 CONC ic convent in the little village of Eerde in South Holland. His health had been badly affected by the tragic simultaneous loss of his wife and elder son, and a broken man he never left the convent until his death in 1958. 
