1 NAME Betsy Clara (Zus) /de Vries/
2 GIVN Betsy Clara (Zus)
2 SURN de Vries
2 _MARNM Goldschmidt
2 NICK Elisabeth
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 22 MAY 1905
2 ADDR
3 CITY Amsterdam
3 STAE North Holland
3 CTRY The Netherlands
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 MAR 1995
2 ADDR
3 CITY Brussels
3 STAE Bruxelles
3 CTRY Belgium
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.famillebutlerdelarochelle.com/devries.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Zus (Betsy), 1905-1995, married - in 1931 - Ernst Goldschmidt (born 1906 in Moravia : then Austria, since 1919 Czech Republic). When arriving in Brussels from Vienna in 1933, Ernst first worked at the Museum for Ancient Art, and t
2 CONC hen started a small art book publishing company (Editions de la Connaissance). He served - as a private - in the Czech forces during the war, first in France, then in England (occasionally organising exhibitions as a sideline) and
2 CONC  then again in France after the Normandy landing. Returning to Belgium, he resumed directing his firm until retirement at 75. Over his lifetime he published many prestigious art books as well as exhibition catalogues, and for abou
2 CONC t 10 years a renowned international contemporary art review (Quadrum). He gave his collection of some 12.000 exhibition catalogues to a French institution, and it is now housed in Marseilles. Zus and Ernst had four children, one o
2 CONC f whom died in infancy. The other three are : Leo ,Paul and Sylvia .
