3 CTRY The Netherlands
1 OCCU Direktor des Rijksmuseum Amsterdam
1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://archief.amsterdam/indexen/deeds/98533455-f704-56a3-e053-b784100ade19
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.monumentsmenandwomenfnd.org/monuments-men-and-women/ary-de-vries
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.famillebutlerdelarochelle.com/devries.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob de Vries, 1905-1983, had a very distinguished career as an art historian, author of many publications (i.a. an expert on Vermeer) and lecturer in all continents. His first position in 1934 was with the Rijksmuseum in Amsterdam
2 CONC . He managed, together with his wife and daughter, to flee Holland during the war and, by way of Belgium and France, crossed over in perilous circumstances into Switzerland. Before the war ended, he was able to reach England where
2 CONC  he was instantly made a major in the allied forces, in order to enable him as an expert to move around in occupied Germany to track down stolen works of art. On return to Holland, he worked again at the Rijksmuseum, where he expe
2 CONC rienced considerable problems in the wake of his denouncing the Vermeers faked by Van Meegeren, until the controversy was definitively resolved to his advantage. He subsequently became Curator of the Mauritshuis in The Hague where
2 CONC  he lived until his retirement, spent in the beautiful manor of Renswoude in central Holland. Bob married Irène de Gunzburg (of the St Petersburg banking family) in 1936 and had two daughters, Nadia and Sacha. 
1 FAMC @F6000000021491126666@
