1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Family: Mainz, Germany, Family Registers 1760-1900, family 12733. Mainz, Germany, Family Registers 1760-1900, Family Number 286.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Mainz, Germany, Births, Marriages and Deaths, 1798-1875, certificate 61.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the year one thousand eight hundred and fifty-five, on May 16th at three o‘clock in the afternoon came to me Franz Bratzig, civil-servant, here at the community hall, the businessman Joseph Simon from Mainz, born in Mainz 7th A
2 CONC ugust 1822, son of the pensioner Johann Simon, 73 years, all persons living in Mainz, and his wife Babette Koch who died November 3rd 1841. The father gave the permission for the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the other side: Babette Seemann, whose name before was Seligmann (name changing), living in Langenschwalbach, born in Langenschwalbach April 27th 1833, adult daughter of the businessman Moses Seemann (before Seligmann) 46 and h
2 CONC is wife Jettchen Mentie, 45, both living in Langenschwalbach were giving their permission.
2 CONT
2 CONT The civil servant said they ( the couple) were giving two announcements of their marriage in front of the community hall, first on 29th april , 11 a.m. and the second on May 6th 1855 in presence of the teacher of religion named Mo
2 CONC rgenthal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nobody said anything against the marriage and so the civil servant declared them as husband and wife . Witnesses were Moses Simon, businessman 41, brother of the groom, Abraham Koch, businessman 27, relative of the mother, Joseph 
2 CONC Richen, policeservant 38, and Mendel Scheppler, civil servant 71, both were no relatives of the couple and the family.
