1 CONT Dr. Joseph L. Bernd: Under a tree from the gravestone “Fredericka Dellevie born August 30, 1784. Wife of Levy Bernd, Hohensohns, Prussia. Died November 29, 1865. (Note spelling of “Dellevie” and “Hohensohns”.) The place of her bir
1 CONC th is also listed but very difficult to make out. I read it “Roiherburg on the Gilda”, but I cannot find this town on my 1902 map of Germany and it could be “Rottenburg on the Neckar”. At any rate, the ravages of time and weather 
1 CONC hade the stone hard to read. Cause of death: pneumonia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Janet Isenberg: With the help of Alan Ehrlich, we have discovered that Fredericka is part of a large family from Rotenberg an der Fulda.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1840 Census - Philadelphia - Kensington Ward
1 CONT 5 males, 3 females
1 CONT
1 CONT 1850 Census - Philadelphia - Middle Ward
1 CONT Levi, Frederica, Adolph, Julius and Amelia
1 CONT House number 857
0 @N6000000007014445060@ NOTE
1 CONT Gustav Carsch - of Carsch Haus fame - a famous department store. ) md. Suzanne Albersheim (for whom I
1 CONT am   named) and they had 6 children: Paul, Else, Hedwig, Walter, Siegfried,
1 CONT and Alice.
1 CONT
1 CONT       Hermann Cars had a son Robert Carsch and Robert had a son Harry.  I do
1 CONT not have names for the wifes of Herman and Robert.
1 CONT
1 CONT Keep me in mind if your ever run across more information for CARS or CARSCH.
1 CONT Thanks again!!!
1 CONT
1 CONT Susan
